📜 FTAI Grammar and Syntax v1.6 — Changelog

Release Date: 2025-04-28
Version: 1.6
Status: Finalized

⸻

🚀 Major Improvements
	•	Emphasis Parsing Resilience:
	•	Parsers must treat unmatched **bold** markers as plain text without error.
	•	Structured Tables Enforcement:
	•	Tables must include a header, --- divider, and maintain consistent column counts.
	•	No blank header cells allowed to ensure deterministic parsing.
	•	Namespace Expansion:
	•	Reserved prefixes expanded to include @sys*, @internal*, @debug*, and @_* for future system and infrastructure tags.
	•	Hierarchy Hardening:
	•	Maximum depth set at two levels (@section, @@subsection).
	•	Deeper structures require external file inclusion via @include.
	•	Type-Hint System Introduced:
	•	Tag suffixes like :int, :float, :bool, :date standardize parsing across implementations.
	•	Clarified Purpose and Core Syntax:
	•	Improved explanations for tags, block closures, quoting behavior, and human-readable emphasis.

⸻

🧠 Guiding Principles Reinforced
	•	Deterministic:
Parsing must always produce the same AST across platforms.
	•	Traceable:
Specifications embed rationale, history, and enable audit integrity.
	•	Minimal:
No unnecessary punctuation or verbose markup.
	•	Composable:
Documents bridge cleanly into JSON, YAML, or other structured data formats.

